course: dictionary
lesson: 6716
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word «offering» is a good example. «The collection is an offering of money for the church's work and for people in need.» Here an offering is money given to help, not a wrapped present.
explain: Look at the words around it. Church, collection and money are the clues. If you put «gift» into the sentence it still sort of fits, but the church clue tells you it means money given during a service.
explain: The same word can also be a verb form. «She is offering to help me with my homework» means she is giving you the chance to take her help. Ask yourself: is the word naming a thing, or showing an action? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: An offering is something you give, especially as a gift.
fact: In church, an offering is money collected during a service, often in a plate or bag while a hymn is sung.
fact: In the Bible, people brought offerings such as animals, grain or the first fruits of the harvest.
fact: «Offering» is the -ing form of the verb «offer», which means giving someone the chance to take something.
fact: An offering can also be something made available to buy or watch, like a new film or a menu choice.
exercise: «The collection is an offering of money for the church's work and for people in need.» What does offering mean here? | A kind of food sold in shops | A trick to fool people | Something you must hide | *Money given to help the church and people in need
exercise: What does offering mean in «She is offering to help me with my homework»? | Money collected in church | A gift wrapped in paper | *Giving someone the chance to take help | Holding something very tightly
exercise: Find and copy one word that means gifts brought to God. «In the Bible, people brought offerings of animals, grain and fruit.» | fruit | people | *offerings | animals
test: «The shop had a new offering: a menu of cheap lunches.» What does offering mean here? | A prayer said in church | *Something made available to buy | A gift wrapped for a birthday | Money given to the poor
test: Which phrase from the lessons means a gift given to make peace? | Harvest moon | Loud noise | Silent sky | *Peace offering
exam: Asha says an offering is always a present in a box. Is she right, using «The collection is an offering of money»? | *No, in church it can mean money given during a service | Yes, but only on birthdays | No, it is only ever a verb | Yes, an offering is always a wrapped present
